# f1, f2, f3 = company.mjs's gray, invert, sepia . f6 = turn . f7, f8, f9 = main.mjs's gray, invert, sepia . L0 = company.mjs's table . L2 = main.mjs's
# A record was one layout for each set of names, for the whole program: the two tables shared three fields, each field held two functions, nothing was proven of it, and `turn` called by
# value what it copies in line where company.mjs is not there (the peer's pixels: 140,833 against 162,436 instructions a turn). How a function is compiled hangs on its own file: a literal
# whose own text writes a method or a function expression under each of its names, a table of functions, has a layout of its file.
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L0.0 "gray" proven=f1 writers-known written-at-construction-alone
# CHECK: field L0.1 "invert" proven=f2 writers-known written-at-construction-alone
# CHECK: field L0.2 "sepia" proven=f3 writers-known written-at-construction-alone
# CHECK: field L2.0 "gray" proven=f7 writers-known written-at-construction-alone
# CHECK: field L2.1 "invert" proven=f8 writers-known written-at-construction-alone
# CHECK: field L2.2 "sepia" proven=f9 writers-known written-at-construction-alone
# RUN(COPY): walk f6:Body mechanisms=all
# COPY-LABEL: code f6:Body
# COPY: frame {{*}} callee=f7
# COPY: frame {{*}} callee=f8
# COPY: frame {{*}} callee=f9
# COPY-NOT: CallDirect
